# Standard perft positions with known node counts.
#
# These are the Phase 1 correctness oracle: movegen is not "done" until every
# line here reproduces exactly. Perft catches almost every legal-move bug there
# is — castling through check, en passant pin edge cases, promotion counting —
# and it catches them deterministically, which no amount of game-playing does.
#
# Source: Chess Programming Wiki, "Perft Results"
#   https://www.chessprogramming.org/Perft_Results
# Node counts transcribed 2026-08-10 and verified twice against that page. They
# were NOT written from memory; if one ever appears to fail, re-check the source
# before assuming the engine is wrong — but assume the engine is wrong first.
#
# Format (the usual perft-suite convention):
#   <FEN> ;D1 <nodes> ;D2 <nodes> ...
#
# Depths are capped at 6. Depth 7+ is documented upstream but takes long enough
# that it belongs in a dedicated run, not in `zig build test-slow`.

# Initial position
rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1 ;D1 20 ;D2 400 ;D3 8902 ;D4 197281 ;D5 4865609 ;D6 119060324

# Position 2 — "Kiwipete". Dense middlegame; the standard castling/pin torture test.
r3k2r/p1ppqpb1/bn2pnp1/3PN3/1p2P3/2N2Q1p/PPPBBPPP/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 1 ;D1 48 ;D2 2039 ;D3 97862 ;D4 4085603 ;D5 193690690 ;D6 8031647685

# Position 3 — sparse endgame; exercises en passant and rook pins.
8/2p5/3p4/KP5r/1R3p1k/8/4P1P1/8 w - - 0 1 ;D1 14 ;D2 191 ;D3 2812 ;D4 43238 ;D5 674624 ;D6 11030083

# Position 4 — promotions under check.
r3k2r/Pppp1ppp/1b3nbN/nP6/BBP1P3/q4N2/Pp1P2PP/R2Q1RK1 w kq - 0 1 ;D1 6 ;D2 264 ;D3 9467 ;D4 422333 ;D5 15833292 ;D6 706045033

# Position 5 — CPW documents this one only to depth 5.
rnbq1k1r/pp1Pbppp/2p5/8/2B5/8/PPP1NnPP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 1 8 ;D1 44 ;D2 1486 ;D3 62379 ;D4 2103487 ;D5 89941194

# Position 6 — quiet, balanced, high branching factor.
r4rk1/1pp1qppp/p1np1n2/2b1p1B1/2B1P1b1/P1NP1N2/1PP1QPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 10 ;D1 46 ;D2 2079 ;D3 89890 ;D4 3894594 ;D5 164075551 ;D6 6923051137
